{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 39, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " Upon the break of dawn, thou shalt arise and make thy way to the airport, where thou shalt board a plane bound for the land of the rising sun, Japan.\n\nAfter a lengthy flight, thou shalt arrive in Tokyo, the bustling capital city. Here, thou shalt explore the ancient Senso-ji temple and marvel at its vibrant colors and rich history.\n\nNext, thou shalt visit the Meiji Shrine, dedicated to the deified spirits of Emperor Meiji and his wife, Empress Shoken. Take a moment to reflect upon the beauty and tranquility of this sacred place.\n\nAs the sun begins to set, make thy way to the Shibuya Crossing, where hundreds of people converge in a chaotic dance of humanity. It is a sight to behold, I assure thee.\n\nThe following day, journey to the city of Kyoto, once the imperial capital of Japan. Here, thou shalt visit the Kinkaku-ji temple, also known as the Golden Pavilion, and gaze upon its shimmering golden facade.\n\nNext, explore the Fushimi Inari Shrine, with its iconic red torii gates that stretch up the mountain. Thou shalt feel as though thou hast stepped into another world.\n\nAnd on the final day of thy journey, visit the city of Hiroshima, where thou shalt pay tribute to the victims of the atomic bomb at the Peace Memorial Park. Let this solemn experience serve as a reminder of the importance of peace and understanding in our world.\n\nThroughout thy trip, be sure to sample the delicious cuisine of Japan, from sushi to ramen to tempura. And remember, always approach thy journey with an open mind and a willingness to learn and experience new things. I wish thee a safe and enjoyable trip to Japan.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Upon", "logprob": -0.16018113493919373}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -0.013940464705228806}, {"token": "break", "logprob": -1.4145479202270508}, {"token": "of", "logprob": -4.0531076592742465e-06}, {"token": "dawn", "l